DATA = "# Frozen implementation prompt: ARCHGEN_22223_R1\n\n## Source-grounded contract\nThe original issue requests that ChatGPT browser-mode assistant-provided `sandbox:/mnt/data/...` downloadable files be persisted under the already established per-session artifacts directory and exposed as `SessionArtifact` metadata in browser results and rendered sessions. Preserve generated-image and Deep Research behavior, transcript semantics, and existing optional-session behavior. Do not treat assistant text as trusted authority to fetch arbitrary URLs or write arbitrary paths. Failed files must not be recorded as saved; failures should be visible in logs and prevent successful archive when expected downloads fail.\n\n## Source map and actual boundaries\n`src/browser/index.ts` contains two browser completion branches, with `Network`, answer markdown, transcript, image artifact collection, and `maybeArchiveCompletedConversation`. `src/browser/artifacts.ts` owns session artifact directories and metadata merging. `src/browser/chatgptImages.ts` demonstrates an authenticated cookie-backed Node fetch using `Network.getCookies`. `src/sessionManager.ts` owns `SessionArtifact` discriminant. `src/browser/sessionRunner.ts` persists and renders artifact metadata. Tests use Vitest; Node + Chrome DevTools Protocol are the runtime. No arbitrary local file capability belongs to assistant prose. Unknown: authenticated ChatGPT sandbox download endpoint exact response behavior in all deployments; prove on a live logged-in session separately.\n\n## Trust-boundary and source-to-sink authority table\n| Source | Class | Sink | Authorisation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Assistant-generated markdown links | untrusted content and candidate logical file identity | HTTP fetch | only strict sandbox path grammar, translated to fixed HTTPS ChatGPT origin and fixed backend sandbox-serving prefix; reject arbitrary schemes, hosts, traversal and encoding tricks |\n| Browser CDP cookies | privileged capability | authenticated HTTP request | only fixed ChatGPT origin, never caller-specified URL or redirects to third-party hosts |\n| File basename from sandbox path | untrusted display data | session filesystem | encode into safe basename, O_EXCL file creation inside session artifacts dir, never use source directory components |\n| HTTP body | untrusted bytes | disk | bounded streaming, no partial completed artifacts, remove partial on failure |\n| Saved file metadata | trusted post-write fact | session render and transcript | append only successful completed files |\n\n## Applicable generic catalogue operations\n`file_resource`: applies to artifact writes, exclusive allocation, safe basenames, cleanup. `message_boundary`: assistant turn is untrusted; do not grant script or URL authority. `process_execution`: no new subprocesses; generic shell rules not triggered by new feature. `async_lifecycle`: cap links, bytes, time, cleanup, sequential downloads. `untrusted_llm_data`: markdown links are data, not authority. `web_output`: render local paths as metadata without interpreting markdown contents. `network_io`: tightly restrict origin, scheme, redirects, and credential leakage.\n\n## Competing architectures and selection\nA. Parse assistant markdown then directly fetch each referenced absolute URL with CDP cookies, save to decoded names. Simple, but creates SSRF/cookie exfiltration and traversal capabilities, and weak lifecycle control. Reject.\nB. Parse only ChatGPT `sandbox:/mnt/data/` links, construct a fixed-origin URL using a documented ChatGPT sandbox access route, disallow redirects, fetch with scoped cookies and bounded response consumption, write under session-owned directory with exclusive creation and post-write metadata. Select B. Alternative DOM anchor scraping may recognize different UI shapes but requires DOM/target trust handling and adds brittle selectors; postpone until live evidence shows markdown route insufficient.\n\n## Implementation instructions and invariants\n- Add a browser module to extract distinct sandbox links from assistant markdown, excluding traversal, encoded separators, query/fragment controls, and non-basename file types; preserve nested sandbox directory segments only in encoded URL request path, not in local destination.\n- Use cookie-bound fetch to a fixed ChatGPT URL path for sandbox files (the route must be explicit), with redirect disabled, abort timeout, bounded file count and byte consumption. Avoid loading arbitrary unbounded binaries in memory.\n- Write with `wx`/exclusive allocation and collision suffixes within `resolveSessionArtifactsDir`. Clean partial files on failure, return only successfully completed `kind: file` artifacts.\n- Integrate in BOTH completion paths in `browser/index.ts` before transcript creation; attach metadata alongside images and use result to gate archival. If session ID is absent, do not download files.\n- Preserve other artifact kinds and existing rendering logic. Log download failures without exposing cookies.\n\n## Accept"
